    "custom_html_8UHbnf": {
      "type": "custom-html",
      "name": "Custom HTML",
      "settings": {
        "subheading": "",
        "title": "",
        "html": "<div class=\"lethical-bb\">\n<div class=\"col-1\">\n<h2 class=\"SectionHeader__Heading Heading u-h3\">Ethical Considerations</h2>\n<p>Reliable, published data around the social impact of laboratory grown diamonds is still developing.</p>\n<p>Areas of uncertainty include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Employment conditions in manufacturing facilities</li>\n<li>Human rights standards across production regions</li>\n<li>Contributions to local communities and economies</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Unlike some mined diamond industries, laboratory grown production does not always have established frameworks for community investment or traceable impact.</p>\n\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-1\">\n<h2 class=\"SectionHeader__Heading Heading u-h3\">Traceability &amp; Transparency</h2>\n<p>Traceability remains one of the most complex aspects of both laboratory grown and natural diamonds.</p>\n<p>Once laboratory grown diamonds enter the global market, identifying their exact origin and production conditions becomes challenging.</p>\n\n<p>At Natalie Marie Jewellery, we apply the same due diligence standards to laboratory grown diamonds as we do to natural diamonds, working only with suppliers who meet our strict requirements.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-1\">\n<h2 class=\"SectionHeader__Heading Heading u-h3\">Certification &amp; Qualit</h2>\n<p>All of our laboratory grown diamonds above 0.30ct are independently certified by leading gemological institutes, including:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>GIA (Gemological Institute of America)</li>\n<li>IGI (International Gemological Institute)</li>\n<li>GCAL (Gem Certification &amp; Assurance Lab)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Each stone features:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A unique certification number</li>\n<li>Detailed grading across cut, colour, clarity and carat</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>"
      }
    },
